From: Anton Argirov <anton.argirov@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:10:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(mmc): encode CSD capacity without an extra unit

CSD version 1 capacity is (C_SIZE + 1) times the block and multiplier unit.
Subtract one when encoding the image size so firmware discovers the actual
medium capacity and does not address a nonexistent trailing unit.

---
diff --git a/src/storage/mmc.c b/src/storage/mmc.c
--- a/src/storage/mmc.c
+++ b/src/storage/mmc.c
@@ -627,7 +627,8 @@
 	mmc_csd[9]=(cmult_8_bits>>1)&3;
 	mmc_csd[0xa]=(cmult_8_bits<<7)&128;
 
-	int device_size=mmc_size[tarjeta]/multiple;
+	/* CSD v1 encodes one less than the number of capacity units. */
+	int device_size=mmc_size[tarjeta]/multiple-1;
 
 	debug_printf (VERBOSE_DEBUG,"device size: %d",device_size);
 
